-- title:
--   Bi-invariance of the mathcal U_q Hecke set under stabiliser units
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ and let $\mathbb H=\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ be the associated quaternion algebra. Let $R$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule of $\mathbb H$ which is an order in the sense of the project predicate [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): $1\in R$, $R$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb Q$-span of $R$ is all of $\mathbb H$, and $R$ is finitely generated. Let $n$ be a unit of $\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\widehat{\mathbb Q}$, where $\widehat{\mathbb Q}$ denotes the finite adèle ring of $\mathbb Q$, and let $q$ be a natural number (no primality is assumed). Write $\widehat\Lambda$ for [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) of a $\mathbb Z$-submodule $\Lambda$, the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $\alpha$ an integral finite adèle, and write $\Lambda^{g}$ for [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31), the preimage in $\mathbb H$ under $x\mapsto x\otimes 1$ of $g\,\widehat\Lambda\,g^{-1}$. Put $S=R\sqcap R^{n}$, the order [`CerednikDrinfeld.meetOrder R n`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_ClassSetGraph.html#L15). Let $u$ be a unit stabilising $\widehat S$ setwise under left multiplication, and let $h$ belong to [`CerednikDrinfeld.uHeckeSet R n q`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_ClassSetGraph.html#L38), that is: $h\in\widehat S$, $q\,h^{-1}\in\widehat S$, $h^{-1}\notin\widehat S$, $q^{-1}h\notin\widehat S$, together with $(R^{n})^{h}=R$ and $R^{h}\neq R^{n}$. Then both $u\,h$ and $h\,u$ again lie in [`CerednikDrinfeld.uHeckeSet R n q`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_ClassSetGraph.html#L38).
--
--   This is the bi-invariance of the $\mathcal U_q$ double coset attached to the intersection order $S=R\cap nRn^{-1}$ under the idelic unit group stabilising $\widehat S$, the statement which makes the associated Hecke correspondence well defined on the double coset space. It is used in the construction of the Hecke laws on the Čerednik–Drinfeld class set graph and in the computation of the edge Hecke operator on joint delta functions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_mul_mem_uHeckeSet_and_mul_mem_uHeckeSet_of_mem_finiteIdeleStabilizer_meetOrder.lean

